{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner product decision P0-1, 2026-10-04: use a purpose-built small project application in its own public source repository as the GitHub-style demo's imported coding target. Provisional working name: artroom-demo-projects. This selects the application kind and repeatable starting state, not a final GitHub account/URL, publication or an Artroom protocol. The public repository URL and exact baseline commit must be recorded by its implementation owner before the deployed run; no repository has been created by this decision.\n\nRequired baseline: a usable application that already lists/views projects, including nonempty projects with tasks, through an HTTP server and browser client; a compact documented build/test command that a clean hosted coding environment and checker can run in a few minutes. The new useful change is Add project export: server produces an honest export of one project's actual data, browser lets the person download it, tests and documentation establish the common interface and recovery behavior. Server, browser, and tests/docs are independently changeable concerns that recombine into one exact reviewed integration commit. Preserve R0's blocking interface request, responsibility handover, failed combined check, independent revision/review, destination-base change, lost publication reply, unrelated-lane progress and leave-A/return-B/watch/steer/review story. A renamed policy fixture or static mock screen does not meet this baseline; actual examples/demo-repo at witnessedb6a9c0b6 contains only two policy files.\n\nKeep Artroom's reusable public packages separate from application code and the demo target. Jam remains its own self-hosting application; its builder capability judgment/vocabulary evolution is unaffected. Do not make Jam construct this coding fixture or require its completion for Jam. Keep the final coding-room application name open; this is not P0-2. This bounded product input can enter the current R2/R4 designs without implying their adoption. Implementation/repository publishing belongs to a concrete owner scope with normal exact review/landing, no root source edits, provider effects or new gate here.","body":{"decision":"P0-1 purpose-built project application","no_git_artifact":"true","repository":"provisional artroom-demo-projects; actual public URL/head owed","scope":"product input; no protocol adoption/source/publication"}}